  "status": "done",
  "options": {
    "brief": "Concrete, accurate facts only: an octopus has one central brain plus a cluster of neurons in each of its 8 arms (often called nine brains); about two-thirds of its roughly 500 million neurons are in the arms; suckers can taste by touch; they solve puzzles and open jars; Inky the octopus escaped New Zealand's National Aquarium in 2016 through a drain pipe; instant camouflage; most live only 1-2 years and learn alone. End on the idea that this intelligence evolved separately from ours."
  },
